{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 90,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- This is a video about\na single simple rule"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3240,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that underpins all of\nphysics, every principle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6720,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from classical mechanics\nto electromagnetism,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10080,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from quantum theory to general relativity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13560,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "right down to the ultimate\nconstituents of matter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16740,
    "dDurationMs": 1593,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the fundamental particles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19620,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All of it can be replaced\nby this single rule."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24030,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It feels like we're\napproaching spooky territory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26100,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- We're approaching spooky territory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27870,
    "dDurationMs": 2013,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I hear you and I agree."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30990,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] It may in fact\nexplain the behavior"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33000,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of life itself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34260,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I think I'm stuck in some\nclassical mindset where, to me,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37260,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the local picture,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38520,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the differential equation way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39840,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of thinking about the universe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41490,
    "dDurationMs": 2013,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that that's really what's going on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46980,
    "dDurationMs": 2433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I fear that I have\nit exactly backwards."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51210,
    "dDurationMs": 2823,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And it all starts with a simple problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55650,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you wanna slide a mass\nfrom point A to point B,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58950,
    "dDurationMs": 3303,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what shape of ramp will\nget it there the fastest?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63270,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is known as the\nproblem of fastest descent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66870,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- You know, common sense, you might say"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68370,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "take the shortest path."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70110,
    "dDurationMs": 1503,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Straight line from A to B."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72720,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] But if you\nbend the ramp down a bit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74640,
    "dDurationMs": 900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the beginning,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75540,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, the mass accelerates\nto a higher speed earlier."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78480,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So even though it\ntravels slightly farther,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80730,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it travels faster and\nbeats the straight ramp."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84270,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the question is, what shape\nprovides the perfect balance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87840,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of acceleration and path length"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90000,
    "dDurationMs": 1773,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to minimize travel time?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92610,
    "dDurationMs": 3033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "According to Galileo, it\nwas the arc of a circle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96540,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He showed that this is\nfaster than any polygon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99600,
    "dDurationMs": 1923,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But is it the fastest?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103950,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nearly 60 years later, in June of 1696,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107250,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Johann Bernoulli set this\nproblem as a challenge"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109920,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the best mathematicians in the world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112770,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Mainly because he's a big show off"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114480,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and he wants to show that\nhe's better than all of them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117840,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] He gave everyone six months"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119610,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to come up with solutions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121260,
    "dDurationMs": 1623,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but none were submitted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124050,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So Gottfried Leibniz, a\nfriend of Bernoulli's,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126420,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "persuaded him to extend the deadline"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128340,
    "dDurationMs": 1893,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to give foreigners a chance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132060,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And I think Newton was\nprobably the intended target"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134400,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because everybody thought\nof him as the best,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136770,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so Johann would've wanted to show"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139050,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that he was better than Newton."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141150,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He was no longer a really active\nmathematician or physicist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145890,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He was working as the warden of the Mint,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148080,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like a big high government position."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150900,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] And on the\n29th of January, 1697,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153750,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Newton returned home\nafter a long day at work"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156300,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to find Bernoulli's challenge in the mail."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159150,
    "dDurationMs": 1627,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Irritated, he wrote,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160777,
    "dDurationMs": 3443,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"I do not love to be dunned\nand teased by foreigners"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164220,
    "dDurationMs": 1887,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about mathematical things.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167190,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the problem was too enticing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169800,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so Newton spent the rest\nof the day and night on it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173970,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and by 4:00 a.m. he had\ncome up with a solution,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177810,
    "dDurationMs": 2433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "something that took Bernoulli two weeks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182250,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Newton submitted his solution"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183690,
    "dDurationMs": 2583,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the journal Philosophical Transactions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187110,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- He sent his solution\nthere but didn't sign it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189540,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And Johann Bernoulli,\nafter seeing the solution,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193380,
    "dDurationMs": 2437,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is alleged to have said,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195817,
    "dDurationMs": 3443,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"I recognize the lion by his claw.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199260,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, that, \"Okay, you\ndon't need to sign it, Newton,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202560,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I can tell who you are."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203940,
    "dDurationMs": 1850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Who else could give such a solution?\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207180,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] And while overall\nNewton dominated Bernoulli,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210630,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in this instance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211860,
    "dDurationMs": 3333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bernoulli's solution\nactually out-shone Newton's."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216330,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I could see why Johann Bernoulli"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218010,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wanted to challenge everybody,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219600,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because he came up with a really clever,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222000,
    "dDurationMs": 3873,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I would say like a truly\ncreative, beautiful solution."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226710,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- To do it, he took inspiration"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228510,
    "dDurationMs": 2793,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from a problem faced by\nancient philosophers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232440,
    "dDurationMs": 2973,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How does light travel\nfrom one place to another?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236490,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This was contemplated\nby Hero of Alexandria"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239040,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the 1st century AD."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241230,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He realized that in a\nsingle medium, like air,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 244290,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "light always follows the shortest path."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247050,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A consequence is that when\nlight reflects, say, off a lake,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250590,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the angle of incidence is always equal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252810,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the angle of reflection."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255030,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Any other path between\nthe start and end points"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257280,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would be longer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258900,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But when light goes from\none medium into another,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261330,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like from air into water,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263010,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it bends in a peculiar way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 265050,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It refracts and it doesn't\nfollow the shortest path."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269280,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- If you've ever dropped something"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270450,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the bottom of a swimming pool"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272280,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you look for it through the water,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274290,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you put your hand in there,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275610,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's not necessarily where you think it is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277620,
    "dDurationMs": 3603,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the light has bent\naway from the flat surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282270,
    "dDurationMs": 2853,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So what is the guiding principle here?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287310,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, over the next 1,600\nyears people slowly figured out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290550,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the sine of the angle of incidence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292860,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "divided by the sine of\nthe angle of refraction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295530,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is equal to a constant, n,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298170,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which depends on the\nnature of the two media."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301260,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This came to be known as Snell's Law."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304020,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But no one knew why it worked."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306930,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, until 1657."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309630,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So another great mathematician"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311190,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "enters our story at this point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312630,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is Pierre Fermat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314310,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By day he was a judge,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316440,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but at night he'd come home"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317940,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and hang out with his wife and kids"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320010,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then do what he really loved the most,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321900,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which was work on math for fun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 324300,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And he mostly worked in pure math"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325830,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but at one point he got\ninterested in the question of,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329460,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why does light obey this\nprinciple of refraction?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334020,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] And he thought\nmaybe Hero of Alexandria"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336840,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was on the right track,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338190,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it's not distance\nthat is being minimized,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340680,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but rather time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342900,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But to see if this was true for refraction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345420,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would be difficult."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346800,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He would have to work out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347940,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every possible path light could take"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 350430,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by varying the point where\nit intersects the boundary"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353280,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and compute the time for each,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355320,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then show that light takes the path"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357360,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for which the total travel\ntime is the shortest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360720,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- He doesn't know how to solve it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 362100,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and he worries that it's\ngonna come out complicated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364620,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even if he could solve it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366210,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so he's not gonna do it. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369270,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think it's 'cause he\nwasn't super interested"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 371190,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in physics, actually."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 372810,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But anyway, years go by,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375180,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he gets interested in it five years later"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377130,
    "dDurationMs": 1110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and tries to solve it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 378240,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then he does solve it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379560,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and he shows that Snell's\nLaw actually pops out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382440,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as the minimizing path\nfor light, you know,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385830,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "under these conditions\nof moving from one medium"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388080,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with one speed of light\nto another with another."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390780,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] And that constant, n,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392460,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, that's just equal\nto the speed of light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394320,
    "dDurationMs": 990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the first medium"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395310,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "divided by the speed of\nlight in the second medium,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397740,
    "dDurationMs": 3423,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which allows us to rewrite\nSnell's Law like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402330,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And he says this thing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403163,
    "dDurationMs": 2197,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I just wanna read you a\nlittle quote 'cause I love it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405360,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He says that this is\n\"the most extraordinary,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408000,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the most unforeseen,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409440,
    "dDurationMs": 2583,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the happiest calculation\" of his life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 413100,
    "dDurationMs": 1473,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "See, it's good to do physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414573,
    "dDurationMs": 2937,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(both laugh)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417510,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you use that principle of least time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 419400,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can explain everything\nthat was known about light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 422250,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the time of Fermat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 424320,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's the first time, as far as I know,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426750,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that anyone shows that nature obeys"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429030,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an optimization principle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 430920,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that nature does the best possible thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 433770,
    "dDurationMs": 3543,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this case, that light takes\nthe shortest possible time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 438450,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] Now, Bernoulli knew"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439680,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about Fermat's principle of least time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441990,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and he thought he could\nuse it to solve the problem"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444510,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of fastest descent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 446460,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- He converted the problem\nfrom a mechanics problem"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 448770,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about a particle sliding down a chute"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451110,
    "dDurationMs": 2733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a problem about optics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455220,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] Instead of a mass\nthat's accelerated by gravity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457830,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he imagined a ray of light\nthat would go faster and faster"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461250,
    "dDurationMs": 3093,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as it went into layers of\nless and less dense media."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465180,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you make the\nlayers thinner and thinner"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467550,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where Snell's Law is\nobeyed at each interface,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 470340,
    "dDurationMs": 2763,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you eventually get a continuous curve."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474240,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now the question is,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 475470,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how should the speed of light change"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477060,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from one layer to the next"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478620,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that it accurately\nmodels a falling object?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481980,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Steven] You could try to\nsolve the problem by thinking,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483780,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if the particle has to fall from A to B,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486150,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's gonna be picking up kinetic energy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488580,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's going faster and faster\nas it slides down the chute"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 491640,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's converting the\nloss in potential energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 494400,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into this kinetic energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495870,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you write down the\nconservation of energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 498180,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for that relationship,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 499770,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you find that the velocity\nthat the particle achieves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503490,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at any time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504323,
    "dDurationMs": 2947,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "having fallen a distance, let's say y,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507270,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its velocity squared will\nbe proportional to y,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 510360,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the height from the top."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 511830,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So velocity goes like\nthe square root of y."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514920,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that'd be sort of like saying"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517290,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "imagine light moving in a way where,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 519780,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "instead of a constant speed of light,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521730,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the speed of light is proportional"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 523500,
    "dDurationMs": 2103,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the distance from the top."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527130,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] Now let's zoom in\nand look at a single interface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 530280,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can plug in our expression"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531750,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the speed of light in each layer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533250,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into Snell's Law."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 534780,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then find that the sine of the first angle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536850,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "divided by the square root\nof y for the first layer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 539520,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is equal to the sine of the second angle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 541350,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "divided by the square root\nof y for the second layer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 544470,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And now here's the key insight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 546570,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Snell's Law also holds for the next layer,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 549330,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and there the ingoing\nangle is simply theta 2."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 552570,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is also equal to\nthe sine of the third angle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 555450,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "divided by the square root of y3."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 557880,
    "dDurationMs": 3843,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the same goes for the next\nlayer and the next and so on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 562980,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 563813,
    "dDurationMs": 4267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this ratio must be equal to\nsome constant, call it k."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568080,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this equation, the story goes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 570330,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bernoulli immediately recognized"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572490,
    "dDurationMs": 2373,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as the equation of a cycloid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 575730,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is the path traced out by a point"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 578190,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "attached to the rim of a rolling wheel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 580950,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is also known as\na brachistochrone curve"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 583830,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the Greek for shortest time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 586800,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Steven] And so the astonishing solution"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 588510,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that the fastest way to get from A to B"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 590790,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is to follow an arc of a cycloid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 593040,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not a circle, a shape called a cycloid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596460,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Now, this curve also has\nanother surprising property."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 599760,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No matter where I release the mass from,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 601830,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it always reaches the\nend at the same time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 604860,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For this reason,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 605820,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's also known as the tautochrone curve,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 608610,
    "dDurationMs": 2403,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the Greek for same time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613020,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Upon finding this solution,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 614550,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bernoulli wrote, \"In this way\nI have solved at one stroke"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618120,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "two important problems,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620010,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an optical and a mechanical one,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 622530,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and have achieved more than\nI demanded from others."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625530,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I have shown that the two problems"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 627420,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "taken from entirely separate\nfields of mathematics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630330,
    "dDurationMs": 1527,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have the same character.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 632700,
    "dDurationMs": 4383,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Little did Bernoulli know he\nwas onto something much bigger."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 638040,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Around 40 years later,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 639390,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one of his students,\nPierre Louis de Maupertuis,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641940,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "also studied the behavior\nof light and particles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 644880,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and he noticed that there are cases"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646590,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where the two behave very similarly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 649590,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This made him think,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650820,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what if Fermat's principle of least time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652980,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wasn't the most fundamental?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 654900,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, why should nature\ncare about minimizing time?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658710,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maybe there is a more foundational\nquantity being minimized,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 662700,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one that doesn't only govern\nlight, but also particles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667440,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, in the 1740s, he\nproposed a new quantity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 670260,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which he called the action."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672600,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is mass times velocity times distance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 676380,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "His thinking went something like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 678600,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The farther something travels,\nthe greater the action."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 681570,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The faster it goes,\nthe greater the action."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684390,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if it's a particle,\nthen the more massive it is,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 687090,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the greater the action."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 689100,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If there are multiple\nsegments to the journey,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691440,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then the total action is just the sum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 693750,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the mass times velocity\ntimes distance for each segment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 698070,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To see the principle in action,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 699810,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "here is a super simple example\nwith no friction or losses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704820,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine a 0.5 kilogram ball\nis rolled over the ground"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708270,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for 6 meters at 3 meters per second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 711270,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then that would be 9 units of action."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 714510,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the ball then bounces"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 715860,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and travels another 6 meters\nat 3 meters per second,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 719220,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then the action for the whole trip"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 721050,
    "dDurationMs": 4203,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is 9 plus 9, or 18 units of action."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 726270,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, what Maupertuis claimed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 727890,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that out of all possible trajectories"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 730170,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where the ball bounces off the wall,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732030,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the path it will follow"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 733350,
    "dDurationMs": 2613,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the one that minimizes the action."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 737880,
    "dDurationMs": 1927,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1744, he wrote,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 739807,
    "dDurationMs": 3443,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"This action is the\ntrue expense of Nature,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 743250,
    "dDurationMs": 3117,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which she manages to make\nas small as possible.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 748140,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what was the response to\nMaupertuis' revolutionary idea?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752730,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He was attacked and ridiculed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 755340,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of his longtime friends,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 756570,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a fellow physicist named Samuel Konig,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 758580,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wrote that \"not only is\nyour principal wrong,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 761670,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you also stole it from Leibniz.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 764340,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Voltaire, who used to be a\nclose friend of Maupertuis,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766800,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "accused him of plagiarism,\nbad physics, being stupid,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 770070,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and just about anything\nelse he could think of."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 772380,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, he wrote a 32-page pamphlet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 774870,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just to mock Maupertuis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 776880,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, this may have\nbeen partly due to rumors"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 778890,
    "dDurationMs": 2673,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Voltaire's lover had an\naffair with Maupertuis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 782910,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But not everyone attacked him."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 785490,
    "dDurationMs": 1983,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some just ignored him."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 788910,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Maupertuis, I've taken\na lot of math and physics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 791610,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in my life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 792443,
    "dDurationMs": 2467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think you're the first person\nI ever heard pronounce it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 794910,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He doesn't get much mention."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 798630,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- All of this was terribly\nstressful for Maupertuis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 801660,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who was nearing the end of his life,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 803730,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and more than anything,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804750,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he thought the principle of least action"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 806640,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would be what he was remembered for."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 808950,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That would be his legacy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 811140,
    "dDurationMs": 4443,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now he was attacked,\nmocked, ridiculed, and ignored."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 817140,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unfortunately, this treatment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 818670,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was at least somewhat justified"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 820830,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because Maupertuis came\nup with this principle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 823080,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by kind of just picking\nit out of thin air."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 826350,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There was no obvious reason\nwhy nature should care"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 829470,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about mass times velocity times distance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 832200,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or even less, why that\nquantity should be minimized."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 836250,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And mathematically, the\nprinciple of least action"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 839010,
    "dDurationMs": 1653,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wasn't rigorous either."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 841830,
    "dDurationMs": 3688,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there was one man who\nvehemently defended it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 845518,
    "dDurationMs": 1985,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that man was Leonhard Euler."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 849390,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first thing Euler did"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 850620,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was he replaced the sum with an integral"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 853320,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so you could calculate the action"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 855180,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while speed or direction\nchanged continuously."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 858570,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And he used this to find\nthe path of a particle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 860940,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around a central mass,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 862590,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like the orbit of a planet around a star."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 865830,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Solving this meant that\nout of every possible path"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 868560,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between two points,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 869850,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he would have to find the one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 870930,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for which the action was the smallest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 873660,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is similar to the\nproblem Fermat tried to solve,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 876780,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only now, instead of\nchanging one variable,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 879270,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he would have to vary every\npossible point along the path,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 882570,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is infinitely many."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 885060,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Needless to say, this was an arduous task."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 887940,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Math had not yet developed the tools"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 889770,
    "dDurationMs": 1953,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "required to handle such problems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 894300,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fortunately, Euler himself\ninvented a new method."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 898620,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was clunky and time\nconsuming, but it worked."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 902280,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Through this process,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 903450,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he realized that the\nprinciple of least action"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 905580,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only works if the total\nenergy is conserved,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 909210,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it is the same for\nall paths considered."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 912810,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These were two conditions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 914190,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that Maupertuis hadn't\nrealized were necessary."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 916890,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So Euler improved the mathematical\nrigor of the principle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 920520,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He found two extra conditions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 922620,
    "dDurationMs": 3153,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and he provided a specific\nexample of it working."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 927000,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Euler is an astonishingly powerful"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 930060,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and not just great mathematician,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 931740,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but appears to be a good guy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 933480,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As far as we could tell,\nhe was very generous."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 936540,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can still read Euler\nand really understand it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 940440,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He helps you, he's empathetic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 942330,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, he was like you are, man."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 944970,
    "dDurationMs": 2043,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He's trying to explain stuff."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 948060,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But Euler was still\nfar from a general proof."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 951600,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That would have to wait for\nanother legendary mathematician,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 955620,
    "dDurationMs": 1923,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Joseph-Louis Lagrange."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 959400,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Joseph-Louis Lagrange\nwas a shy 19-year-old,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 962310,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mostly self-taught."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 964110,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But despite his age,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 965310,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he was already working at\nthe forefront of mathematics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 968250,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "including with Euler's new method."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 970620,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1754, he shared his results with Euler,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 973680,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who replied that Lagrange\nhad \"extolled the theory"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 976290,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the highest summit of perfection,\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 978810,
    "dDurationMs": 2247,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which caused him \"the greatest joy.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 982290,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But besides being world\nclass mathematicians,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 984690,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the two had another thing in common."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 986820,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They were both huge proponents"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 988620,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the principle of least action."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 990630,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And around five years later,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 992310,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just a year after Maupertuis' death,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 994860,
    "dDurationMs": 3183,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lagrange succeeded in\nproviding a general proof."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1000560,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is there any intuitive\nway to think about action?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1004260,
    "dDurationMs": 3050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I feel like there's an intuitive\nway to think about force"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1007310,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and there's kind of an intuitive\nway to think about energy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1010520,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but is there an intuitive\nway to think about action?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1013190,
    "dDurationMs": 990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I don't know."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1014180,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I wanna watch your show to learn."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1016610,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I hope you'll come up with it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1017780,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because I don't have a\ngood feeling about action."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1021380,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] Now I wanna\nexplain Lagrange's proof,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1023660,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but I don't want to do it the way he did."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1026270,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So instead, we'll go through three steps."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1028910,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First we'll explain the general approach"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1030860,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Euler and Lagrange came up with."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1032810,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then we'll rewrite the\nprinciple into its modern form."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1036140,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And finally we'll apply this\nmath to a simple example"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1039290,
    "dDurationMs": 2163,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to show you why it works."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1043010,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So first, the general approach."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1045380,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If there are infinite possible paths,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1047960,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how do you find the one\nwith the least action?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1050870,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, Euler and Lagrange\nrealized you can do it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1053450,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a similar way to how you\nfind the minimum of a function."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1057140,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There you take the derivative\nand set it equal to 0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1060680,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And where the slope is horizontal,\nthat must be the minimum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1064970,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you took a tiny step\nto the left or the right,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1068420,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the value of the function\nbasically doesn't change."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1071690,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And similarly, if you have\nthe path of least action,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1075440,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then if you were to change it a little bit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1077630,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by, say, adding a tiny bump\nhere or flattening it out there,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1081530,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "imagine we're just adding\na tiny function, eta,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1084590,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to our path of least action,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1086390,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, then the action\nbasically shouldn't change"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1089660,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because we're at this\nreally special point,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1092030,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the path of least action."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1094220,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You add a little bit to the minimal path"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1096200,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the action is still the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1097520,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If that is the optimal path\nthat has the least action,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1100190,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then any other path must have more action."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1103340,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So the counter there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1104870,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is like all of this is the first order."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1107360,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you're looking at linear terms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1109850,
    "dDurationMs": 2613,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that are proportional\nto eta, the deviation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1112463,
    "dDurationMs": 1377,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then the first order,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1113840,
    "dDurationMs": 1013,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the difference in action will be 0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1114853,
    "dDurationMs": 2167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the way you could imagine this is like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1117020,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "let's say you're at the bottom of a bowl"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1118790,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you're at the minimum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1120110,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you make some tiny step\naway and we call that step eta."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1123410,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If that change would\nbe proportional to eta,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1125510,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you would maybe increase on this side"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1127310,
    "dDurationMs": 1110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but decrease on this side"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1128420,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then this would no\nlonger be a minimum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1130430,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So sort of the coefficient\nof eta has to be 0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1134600,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But since you're at a minimum,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1136010,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it kind of goes like a parabola,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1138080,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it can be proportional to eta squared"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1139940,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or potentially some higher order term."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1141800,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So there is a tiny\ndeviation in the action,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1145400,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it's not proportional to eta."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1147410,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the first order,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1149120,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the change in action\nbetween the optimal path"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1151520,
    "dDurationMs": 1983,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and some trial path is 0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1155090,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So what you can write"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1156350,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that the action of this trial path"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1158390,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "minus the action of the true path"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1160310,
    "dDurationMs": 2613,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is equal to 0 to first order."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1164000,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a compact way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1165560,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of writing the principle of least action,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1167780,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's the general approach you use"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1169640,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to solve all these problems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1172250,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So with that in hand,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1173390,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "let's rewrite the principle\ninto its modern form,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1176420,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "starting with Maupertuis' action,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1178430,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is the sum of mass\ntimes velocity times distance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1182360,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Euler changed this into an integral,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1184190,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it's the integral\nof mass times velocity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1186680,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "integrated over distance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1188840,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now the velocity is equal to ds over dt,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1192140,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which we can rearrange\nto get ds equals vdt."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1195500,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And plugging this in,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1196790,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we have an integral of\nmv squared over time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1200570,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But wait, that's just\ntwice the kinetic energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1203570,
    "dDurationMs": 930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as Euler pointed out,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1204500,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the total energy must be conserved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1206990,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Total energy is just\nkinetic plus potential."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1210050,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we can rewrite this\nas T equals E minus V."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1214490,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And filling this in for\nthe second T gives us"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1216830,
    "dDurationMs": 4950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the variation of T plus\nE minus V integrated over time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1221780,
    "dDurationMs": 1563,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is equal to 0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1224330,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now we can split this integral into two,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1226610,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and since the energy is constant,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1228380,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can integrate this term\nover time to get this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1231980,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we can simplify this even further."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1234110,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just like with a normal derivative,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1235760,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can write the variation of E times t"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1238340,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as E times the variation of t"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1240200,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plus t times the variation of E."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1242690,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But remember, as Euler found,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1244400,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the energy of different\npaths has to be the same,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1247250,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the variation between them is 0"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1249530,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this term drops out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1251750,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we rearrange this like so,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1253670,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then we find that the\nvariation of this integral"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1256010,
    "dDurationMs": 4443,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is equal to minus the energy\ntimes the variation of time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1261560,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This looks a lot like some\nother minimization principle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1264920,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if only this was equal to 0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1267530,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, we can make this 0"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1269330,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by only considering paths that\nhave the same travel time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1272750,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you do that, then there's\nno longer any variation in time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1276350,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this term drops out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1278330,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what we find is that\nMaupertuis' principle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1281000,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has changed into another form"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1283580,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where now the variation of kinetic energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1286340,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "minus potential energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1287960,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "integrated over time is equal to 0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1291320,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- T minus V, kinetic energy\nminus potential energy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1295250,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then you integrate that along a path"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1297770,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that you're traveling from A to B,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1299300,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then integrate it\nwith respect to time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1301490,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's all very strange"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1302720,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and yet that turns out to be\nthe correct thing to integrate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1306710,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] Now this is a little weird."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1308120,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We started with mass times velocity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1310160,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "integrated over distance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1311570,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and now we have the kinetic energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1313070,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "minus the potential energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1314480,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "integrated over time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1316250,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And somehow both are ways"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1318020,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to write the principle of least action."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1320540,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that also means\nthat this integral here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1322670,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "T minus V integrated over time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1324440,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is another way to write the action."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1327200,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first person"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1328033,
    "dDurationMs": 1897,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to write the principle\nof least action like this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1329930,
    "dDurationMs": 3345,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was William Rowan Hamilton in 1834,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1333275,
    "dDurationMs": 3615,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and by doing so, he got the\nprinciple named after him."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1336890,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So the principle of least action"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1338810,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that we write as integral of Ldt,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1341750,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "L being being the Lagrangian,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1343400,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the T minus V, the kinetic\nminus potential energy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1346370,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they don't call it Lagrange's Principle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1348050,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they call it Hamilton's Principle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1350000,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I guess Hamilton is building\non Lagrange in that way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1353810,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Hamilton's Principle is the modern way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1355970,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of writing the principle of least action"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1357950,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the way you'd find it in\nalmost every physics book."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1360890,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In part that's because\nHamilton's Principle tells you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1363230,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how objects move from one place to another"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1366020,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rather than just giving\nyou the shape of the path."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1369170,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Two other important differences\nbetween both principles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1371630,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are that the action is\nnow an integral over time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1374480,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "instead of space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1375680,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And a consequence is that\nwith Hamilton's Principle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1378200,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you now need a start and end point,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1380150,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and also a start and end time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1383210,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The third is that with\nMaupertuis' principle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1385520,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you need to keep the energy\nof different paths the same,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1388880,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the time can vary."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1390500,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While with Hamilton's Principle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1391910,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the energies can differ"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1393290,
    "dDurationMs": 2643,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the time has to be\nthe same between paths."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1397820,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So now we have our general approach"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1399920,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the modern way of\nwriting the principle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1401780,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so let's apply it to a simple\nexample to see why it works."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1405950,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's say I throw this ball\nstraight up in the air,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1409520,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it goes from some start point"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1411620,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to say a different end point\nin a certain amount of time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1415910,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now if we call the height\nof the ball y of t,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1418910,
    "dDurationMs": 2847,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then we can plot these two points like so,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1421757,
    "dDurationMs": 1893,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then we can imagine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1423650,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "infinitely many possible trajectories"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1426020,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that could connect these two points."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1427760,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some go a little higher, some lower,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1430430,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some have wiggles, others don't."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1432860,
    "dDurationMs": 1110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The only condition"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1433970,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that all paths must have\nthe same start and end point"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1437360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the same amount of\ntime elapsed between them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1440360,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now to find the real trajectory,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1442160,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we proceed as before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1444110,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We imagine that this is\nthe true path, y of t,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1447110,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the one with the least action."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1448910,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then we imagine making\nsmall variations to it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1451820,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by pushing it up a little here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1453650,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "down a little there, and so on,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1455870,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "making tiny changes at every time step,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1458510,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which we'll call eta of t."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1460760,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when you add y and eta together,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1463130,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get this new trial path,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1464810,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "let's call it q of t."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1466820,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And since the variations are small,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1468800,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the difference in action\nbetween these two paths is 0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1472610,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Our next task is to solve this equation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1476240,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we compute the action for each path."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1478910,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For this, we need the kinetic\nand potential energy for each,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1481850,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we write them as a\nfunction of y and eta."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1485270,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Plugging that in,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1486103,
    "dDurationMs": 3607,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get the difference in\nactions is equal to this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1489710,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But wait, this first integral"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1491540,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is just the action of the true path,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1493550,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so these integrals cancel,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1495560,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and what you're left with is just that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1498500,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "m times dy over dt"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1500420,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "times d eta over dt"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1502220,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "minus eta times the\nderivative of the potential"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1505100,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "integrated over time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1506600,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is equal to 0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1508580,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can rewrite this further\nby using integration by parts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1511970,
    "dDurationMs": 3843,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That allows us to replace\nthis term with this one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1517130,
    "dDurationMs": 990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if we plug that in,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1518120,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we now have some function"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1519680,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that when multiplied by eta\nand integrated over time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1522590,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has to be equal to 0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1524570,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But since eta can be just about anything,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1527120,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this can only be true if this part is 0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1531110,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what we found is that the\naction is minimal for the path"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1534500,
    "dDurationMs": 3783,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that satisfies this curious\ndifferential equation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1539660,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now it might look\ncomplicated, but it's not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1543080,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Minus the derivative of the\npotential is just the force."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1547370,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the second derivative of height?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1549770,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, that's just acceleration."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1552320,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if we rearrange this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1554000,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we find that the path that satisfies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1555860,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the principle of least action"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1557600,
    "dDurationMs": 2973,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the one that obeys F equals ma."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1564050,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words, the principle\nof least action is equivalent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1567440,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to Newton's Second Law,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1569930,
    "dDurationMs": 2433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it covers more than just mechanics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1574520,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fermat's principle of least time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1575990,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "turned out to be nothing\nmore than a special case"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1578420,
    "dDurationMs": 1713,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the principle of least action."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1581810,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So with this single principle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1583700,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you could suddenly describe everything,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1585560,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from light reflecting and refracting,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1588320,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the swinging of a pendulum clock,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1590720,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to planets orbiting the sun"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1592310,
    "dDurationMs": 2763,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and stars orbiting the core of the galaxy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1595910,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What used to be viewed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1596990,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as entirely separate fields of physics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1599450,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were now all unified under\na single simple rule."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1603710,
    "dDurationMs": 2733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The variation of the action is 0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1608270,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After Euler found out\nabout Lagrange's proof,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1610490,
    "dDurationMs": 1387,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he wrote to him,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1611877,
    "dDurationMs": 2633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"How satisfied would\nnot Mr. Maupertuis be,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1614510,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were he still alive,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1615950,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if he could see his\nprinciple of least action"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1618050,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "applied to the highest degree of dignity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1620030,
    "dDurationMs": 1737,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to which it is susceptible.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1628700,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With Lagrange's proof,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1630260,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we now have two ways to\nsolve any mechanics problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1633740,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can either use forces and vectors"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1636020,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or you can use energies and scalars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1638750,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It seems like the\nprinciple of least action"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1640820,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is just way too complicated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1642710,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is so unnecessary."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1644510,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Who would ever use this, you know,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1646190,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when you could just use\nNewton's Second Law?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1647660,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like that's a piece of cake."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1649400,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Your options are either use all of this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1653060,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or just start with F equals ma,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1654590,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they give you the same answer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1655910,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why ever use the\nprinciple of least action?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1658310,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, that's because Euler and\nLagrange came up with a way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1661370,
    "dDurationMs": 2763,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to make all of this like\nsuper, super simple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1664970,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] If this is the action,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1666800,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then T minus V is called the Lagrangian."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1669980,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now let's replace everything we did before"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1672170,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the Lagrangian."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1674150,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then you see that the\nprinciple of least action works"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1676790,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whenever this differential\nequation is satisfied."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1680090,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So all you have to do now"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1681590,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you wanna solve any mechanics problem"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1684050,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is you just write down the\nkinetic and potential energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1686930,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you plug it into this\nequation and you're done."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1690950,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that becomes extremely powerful."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1694490,
    "dDurationMs": 997,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I remember thinking,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1695487,
    "dDurationMs": 2723,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Man, force is like hard\nto get the right answer.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1698210,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can do it if you're good,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1699620,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and people who are good\nat mechanics can do it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1701960,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But with the Lagrangian approach,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1703730,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you have this machine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1705290,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "crank out the principle\nof least action on it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1707780,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you get the right equation to motion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1709460,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you don't have to be a good physicist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1711320,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That was what I took from it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1712970,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that as a math guy I can do physics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1715250,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thanks to Lagrange and Euler."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1717350,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And it doesn't just\nwork in one dimension."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1719870,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you have more dimensions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1721400,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then you just solve the\nEuler-Lagrange equation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1723980,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for each coordinate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1725720,
    "dDurationMs": 1110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Another thing that's great is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1726830,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you could use weird coordinate systems"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1728810,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that might be better\nsuited to the problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1731090,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like if you were doing a\nproblem with something rotating,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1733850,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you might want to use polar coordinates"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1736070,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "instead of Cartesian coordinates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1737960,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this will give you the\ncorrect equations of motion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1740210,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in polar coordinates,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1741830,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which again might be kind of\ntricky to do with vectors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1744920,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Derek] Like with the double pendulum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1746660,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Trying to solve this using\nforces is extremely hard."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1750020,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Because as one pendulum is swinging,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1752150,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it provides the attachment point"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1753710,
    "dDurationMs": 1317,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the pendulum hanging below it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1755027,
    "dDurationMs": 2673,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so that pendulum is in\nthis moving reference frame"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1757700,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as it's swinging."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1758900,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a very nasty job to write\ndown the correct F equals ma"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1763040,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for a double pendulum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1764870,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you write it down with\nkinetic and potential energy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1767750,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's pretty easy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1769250,
    "dDurationMs": 3213,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- This is actually how\nwe made this simulation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1773690,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, there is one little side note"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1775760,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we should give about the\nprinciple of least action,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1777770,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the name is a little misleading."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1780950,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Although we often refer to the principle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1783110,
    "dDurationMs": 2163,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as the principle of least action,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1786170,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's probably good to\nadd a little caveat here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1789140,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that sometimes it's not\nnecessarily the minimum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1792020,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just as when you find in calculus"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1793880,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when you set a derivative to 0,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1795650,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that doesn't guarantee\nyou're getting the minimum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1797660,
    "dDurationMs": 1050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of a function."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1798710,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The principle of least\naction more properly stated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1801440,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "should be the principle\nof stationary action."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1803960,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That the laws of motion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1804980,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "come from demanding a stationary point,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1807170,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is tantamount to this condition"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1809180,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of setting a certain derivative to 0"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1811460,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then getting the\nEuler-Lagrange equation from that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1814760,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So very often it is a true\nminimum, but not always."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1819500,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But action is much more fundamental"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1821810,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than just classical mechanics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1823910,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Around the turn of the 20th century,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1825890,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "action popped up as the\nkey part of a solution"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1828620,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to one of the biggest\nproblems in atomic physics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1830870,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1831890,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The UV catastrophe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1834020,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It's kind of spooky\nthat this breakthrough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1838010,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that starts the ball rolling\ntoward quantum theory"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1840920,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "brings action in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1842210,
    "dDurationMs": 2553,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not energy and not force, action."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1846440,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It gives you a hint, yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1849110,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But that and much more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1851300,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will have to wait for a separate video,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1853400,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so make sure you're subscribed"
